    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday is a publicly traded enterprise software company, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, CA, that provides cloud-based applications for human resources, finance, and IT. The company trades on the ticker WDAY and reported revenue of $9,552,000,000 for the fiscal year ending January 31, 2026, according to its most recent 10-K filing. Its SEC CIK is 0001327811.\n\nThe company describes itself as offering an enterprise AI platform and positions its core product, Workday AI, as a system that activates teams of specialized agents to perform processes across HR, finance, and IT. The site highlights agentic AI developed in collaboration with Sana, emphasizing capabilities it characterizes as the ability to find, build, act, and automate rather than merely assist. Workday AI is categorized as an ERP and business application AI product, covering skills-based talent management, predictive analytics, and sensitive HR data handling.\n\nWorkday is named as a defendant in nine federal civil cases across multiple jurisdictions, including the Eastern District of California, the Northern District of Georgia, the Northern District of California, the District of Colorado, the District of Maryland, and the Eastern District of Virginia. Notable cases include Williams v. Workday, Inc. in the Northern District of Georgia and Elias v. Workday, Inc. in the Northern District of California, alongside several matters brought by pro se plaintiffs.",
